note The handler, on the frame the button is let go. Nothing happens unless the grab moved and landed on another row. Under: the row's step is the new parent and the step goes to the end of the list. Before: the row's parent, placed ahead of the row. After: the row's parent, placed ahead of the next sibling after the row in list order, or at the end. The map moves it; every slot of the path is remapped by id, since a move changes list positions; the status names the new number and parent.

